jank-28: untyped params speculated as i64: a native entry beside the generic body, picked per call
(cohost doc/upstream/jank-28-param-speculation.md; lane U6, order U6-3)

Base: jank-lang/jank f3d82d65499920f81216e9235bd5d3a34a968e3f with the series before it in
upstream/jank/patches/series (11, 13, 14, 12-21, 18, 19, 15a-16, 15b-17, 22, 20, 23, 24, 26). Apply
from the clone's root: git apply <this file>.

Builds on 20-native-returns (native entry per typed arity, boxing entry, named recursion and typed
call sites into it) for fns with no hints at all.

Files:
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/analyze/processor.cpp, include .../analyze/processor.hpp,
  .../analyze/expr/function.hpp:
  - speculation_candidate: a syntactic filter: an arity with an untyped param that appears
    directly in a numeric operation ((< n 2), (dec n), (+ acc i), ...) or in a binding vector
    ((loop [i n] ...)); most fns are analyzed once as before.
  - analyze_fn, with_speculation: such an arity that got no native entry is analyzed a second time
    with its untyped params as i64 (analyze_fn_arity's speculate_params). If that gives a native
    entry (20's rules: a native-number tail, no fn-level recur), the arity is speculative and the
    first analysis is kept as its generic twin (function_arity::generic, fn_ctx->generic_twin).
    Closures keep their generic arities.
  - analyze_call: named recursion into a speculative arity, and a typed call site to one, call the
    native entry only when every argument is a native number of the parameter's kind; any other
    argument (an object, which may be a real, a ratio or a string) goes through the boxing entry.
    So nothing throws that did not throw before.
  - the native-entry registry (typed call sites, 20) records the speculative flag.
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/ir/processor.cpp, builder.cpp, include .../ir/builder.hpp,
  .../ir/instruction.hpp: the generic twin is an IR function <name>_<n>_generic, emitted as a
  module entry point (root fn) or with its function instruction (nested fns, as in AOT modules).
- compiler+runtime/src/cpp/jank/codegen/cpp_processor.cpp: a speculative arity's boxing entry
  <name>_<n> calls <name>_<n>_native when every speculated argument is an integer (a tagged small
  integer or an integer object) and <name>_<n>_generic otherwise; the generic twin is emitted
  under its own name. Overflow stays checked in the native entry (12-21's arms).

Not done here (named for the next order): an f64 variant. A fn whose untyped params arrive as reals
(H0's down-double-plain, called with 2000000.0) takes the generic body, as before: 8784249 ->
8757379 ns.

